From aeac57d2c96c6ed3cf443d978d181db30863d6c0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 04:55:33 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(cron): bound repeated raw quote expansion in lifecycle
 walks [daveey]

Why: HOME expansion exposes a benign wrapper graph whose overlapping quoted
output spans recursively enumerate pairs already enumerated by their parent.
The repeated work exhausts the shared 16384-line budget, despite no lifecycle
action. The old baseline misses the newly HOME-reachable helper entirely.

Carry explicit raw-quote provenance and an immutable interpretation snapshot.
Only omit contained quote enumeration for unchanged raw spans in the same
cwd/execution/alias/masking scope. Continue scanning every payload and file;
decoded strings, printer assembly and shell command payloads keep full expansion.
Move output expansion to a topical sibling; caps and path safety are unchanged.

Proof: reduced budget regression is red without coverage and green with it;
9 exact-anchor mutants killed; 2063 lifecycle/backend tests and 1719 additional
focused/cross-cutting tests passed (overlapping selections). All 20 checks pass.
Unmemoized 54-input frozen same-byte replay of baseline, HOME PR and HOME+fix
clears exactly core-wt indices 181/182/2366. The separate gh-shim log refusal
at index6985 remains, traced to disabled date exemption after PATH/source
changes; HOME owner retains that gate and complete final 7052-input replay.
No stored commands were executed; referenced-file cache remains private.
